{%- liquid
  # THE SHELL WRAPS WHAT IT CAN REACH. Four of the six documents the sidebar
  # lists — privacy, refund, cancellations, contact information — are Shopify
  # SHOP POLICIES, served from checkout.shopify.com in Shopify's own bare
  # template. No theme can style them. So this shell dresses the pages the
  # theme does own (shipping & returns, privacy choices) and links out to the
  # rest, which at least makes the set navigable as one thing.
  #
  # Moving the hosted policies into ordinary pages would bring them inside the
  # shell, but it duplicates legal text into a second place that can drift from
  # the one checkout links to. Not doing that silently — see LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.
  assign policy_stamp = page.metafields.caddieinsight.last_updated.value | default: page.published_at

  assign summary = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'summary'
  assign links = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'link'
-%}

<div class="sl-wrap sl-policy">
  <nav class="sl-policy__crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span>{{ section.settings.crumb | default: 'Policies' }}</span>
  </nav>

  <div class="sl-policy__grid">
    {%- comment -%}
      The index is a <nav> and comes FIRST in the DOM, before the document it
      indexes, so a screen reader meets the set before the page. It is ordered
      visually second on desktop by grid placement rather than by source order.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <nav class="sl-policy__aside" aria-label="{{ section.settings.crumb | default: 'Policies' | escape }}">
      {%- if links.size > 0 -%}
        <p class="sl-mono-label">{{ section.settings.aside_label | default: 'Policies' }}</p>
        <ul class="sl-policy__index" role="list">
          {%- for block in links -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign url = block.settings.url
              if url == blank and block.settings.page != blank
                assign url = block.settings.page.url
              endif
            -%}
            {%- if url != blank -%}
              {%- assign is_here = false -%}
              {%- if block.settings.page != blank and block.settings.page.handle == page.handle -%}
                {%- assign is_here = true -%}
              {%- endif -%}
              <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <a href="{{ url }}"
                   class="sl-policy__index-link{% if is_here %} is-current{% endif %}"
                   {% if is_here %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ block.settings.label }}</a>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            The Shopify-hosted ones, resolved through the shop object rather
            than pasted in as checkout.shopify.com URLs — those carry the shop
            id and the policy id, and a merchant copying one by hand is how a
            policy link ends up pointing at another store's document. Each
            renders only if that policy has actually been written.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if section.settings.show_shop_policies -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              shop.policies, not a concat chain of shop.privacy_policy and
              friends: `concat` takes arrays, each of those is a single object,
              and the chain silently yields nothing — the index rendered with
              no hosted policies at all and looked merely short rather than
              broken. shop.policies is already the array, and it only contains
              the policies that have been written.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for policy in shop.policies -%}
              {%- if policy.url != blank -%}
                <li>
                  <a href="{{ policy.url }}" class="sl-policy__index-link">{{ policy.title }}</a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.help_body != blank -%}
        <div class="sl-policy__help sl-blueprint">
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--tl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--tr" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--bl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <i class="sl-corner sl-corner--br" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <p class="sl-policy__help-title">{{ section.settings.help_title | default: 'Question about an order?' }}</p>
          <p class="sl-policy__help-body">{{ section.settings.help_body }}</p>
          {%- assign contact_page = pages['contact'] -%}
          {%- if contact_page.url != blank -%}
            <a class="sl-btn sl-btn--outline sl-btn--sm" href="{{ contact_page.url }}">Contact support</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </nav>

    <div class="sl-policy__main">
      {%- if policy_stamp != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A dateline, not decoration. On a refund policy the date IS part of
          the terms — it is how a customer knows which version they agreed to
          — so it is a <time> with a machine-readable datetime rather than a
          formatted string.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="sl-policy__stamp">
          Last updated
          <time datetime="{{ policy_stamp | date: '%Y-%m-%d' }}">{{ policy_stamp | date: '%d %b %Y' | upcase }}</time>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h1 class="sl-policy__title">{{ section.settings.heading | default: page.title }}</h1>

      {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-policy__intro">{{ section.settings.intro }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if summary.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The terms at a glance, above the prose. Somebody arriving here wants
          one number — how long have I got — and making them read four numbered
          clauses to find it is how a policy page becomes a support ticket.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <dl class="sl-policy__summary">
          {%- for block in summary -%}
            <div class="sl-policy__summary-cell" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <dt>{{ block.settings.label }}</dt>
              <dd>
                <b>{{ block.settings.value }}</b>
                {%- if block.settings.note != blank -%}
                  <span>{{ block.settings.note }}</span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </dd>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </dl>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="sl-policy__body sl-rte">{{ page.content }}</div>

      {%- if section.settings.footer_note != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-policy__foot">{{ section.settings.footer_note }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
.sl-policy { padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 72px; }
.sl-policy__crumb {
  display: flex;
  gap: var(--sl-space-2);
  margin-bottom: var(--sl-space-6);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-policy__crumb a { color: inherit; }

.sl-policy__grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-7);
  align-items: start;
}
/* The index is first in the DOM so it is met before the document; on desktop
   it is placed into the second column instead, which keeps the reading order
   for assistive tech and the visual order for everyone else. */
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-policy__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 260px); gap: var(--sl-space-8); }
  .sl-policy__aside { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; position: sticky; top: var(--sl-space-6); }
  .sl-policy__main { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
}

.sl-policy__index { margin: var(--sl-space-3) 0 var(--sl-space-6); padding: 0; list-style: none; }
.sl-policy__index li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border); }
.sl-policy__index-link {
  display: block;
  padding: var(--sl-space-3) 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.sl-policy__index-link:hover { color: var(--sl-ink); }
.sl-policy__index-link.is-current { color: var(--sl-ink); font-weight: var(--sl-weight-medium); }

.sl-policy__help { padding: var(--sl-card-inset); background: var(--sl-orange-soft); }
.sl-policy__help-title { margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-2); font-weight: var(--sl-weight-medium); font-size: var(--sl-text-sm); }
.sl-policy__help-body { margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-4); color: var(--sl-ink-soft); font-size: var(--sl-text-sm); line-height: 1.5; }

.sl-policy__stamp {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-3);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-policy__title { margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-4); color: var(--sl-ink); }
.sl-policy__intro {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-6);
  max-width: 62ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.sl-policy__summary {
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-7);
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
@media (min-width: 560px) { .sl-policy__summary { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
.sl-policy__summary-cell { padding: var(--sl-dense-inset); background: var(--sl-bg-card); }
.sl-policy__summary-cell dt {
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-policy__summary-cell dd { margin: var(--sl-space-2) 0 0; display: grid; gap: 2px; }
.sl-policy__summary-cell dd b { color: var(--sl-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-display); font-size: var(--sl-text-2xl); font-weight: var(--sl-weight-display); line-height: 1; }
.sl-policy__summary-cell dd span { color: var(--sl-ink-soft); font-size: var(--sl-text-sm); }

.sl-policy__body { max-width: 68ch; }
.sl-policy__foot {
  margin: var(--sl-space-7) 0 0;
  padding-top: var(--sl-space-4);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  max-width: 68ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.55;
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Policy page",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb", "label": "Breadcrumb label", "default": "Policies" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "info": "Leave blank to use the page title." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "intro", "label": "Intro" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The date comes from the page's caddieinsight.last_updated metafield, falling back to its publish date. On a policy the date is part of the terms — it is how a customer knows which version they agreed to."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Index" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "aside_label", "label": "Index label", "default": "Policies" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_shop_policies",
      "label": "List Shopify's own policies too",
      "info": "Privacy, refund, shipping, cancellations and terms, resolved automatically. They are served by Shopify and cannot be styled by the theme.",
      "default": true
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Help card" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "help_title", "label": "Title", "default": "Question about an order?" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "help_body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "Include the order number from your confirmation email and we can answer in one reply."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Footer" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "footer_note", "label": "Footer note" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "name": "Summary cell",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Memberships" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "value", "label": "Value", "default": "14 days" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "note", "label": "Note", "default": "If unused" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "link",
      "name": "Index link",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label" },
        { "type": "page", "id": "page", "label": "Page", "info": "Used for the link and to mark the current item." },
        { "type": "url", "id": "url", "label": "URL", "info": "For Shopify-hosted policies, which have no page object." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Policy page" }]
}
{% endschema %}
